<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Naha</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Naha is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/okinawa-prefecture">Okinawa Prefecture</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, on the south-west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/okinawa-island">Okinawa Island</a>. It grew as the port of the Ryukyu Kingdom, handling tribute trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and trade with Japan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> and South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>, below the royal castle of Shuri, which is now part of the city. Badly damaged in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-okinawa">Battle of Okinawa</a> in 1945, it was the seat of the US administration of Okinawa until 1972.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/naha.jpg" alt="Naha" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 663highland nnh Composition by Kyoww · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naha_montage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
